  "id": "COMPOUND:22056 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between the compound in question and LS174T, mediated through Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Jionoside D and 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol, all of which are known to interact with LS174T. The consistent presence of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a target across these pathways indicates a central role in the mechanism of action. The evidence supports a pathway where the compound may act as a modulator of this protein, potentially influencing LS174T through interactions involving microtubule dynamics. The integration of multiple targets and their shared interaction with LS174T highlights a possible mechanism of action involving microtubule-associated proteins, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
